---
import CourseHome from '../../../../components/course/CourseHome.astro';
import '../../../../styles/lesson-kit.css';
import { SKYWATCH } from '../../../../courses/sky-watching/syllabus';
---
<CourseHome course={SKYWATCH}>
  <p class="cs-meta"><strong>Quick reference:</strong> <a href="/learn/courses/sky-watching/glossary/">glossary of terms</a> · <a href="/learn/courses/sky-watching/cheat-sheet/">formula cheat sheet</a></p>
  <section class="cs-builds">
    <h2>What you will be able to do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Find your way around the sky</strong> with no gear: the turning sky, seasons, the Moon, the planets, constellations and star brightness.</li>
      <li><strong>Point at anything</strong> with altitude and azimuth, right ascension and declination, sidereal time and Julian dates.</li>
      <li><strong>Get the most from a dark sky</strong>: dark adaptation, light pollution, seeing and planning a night.</li>
      <li><strong>Choose and use binoculars, a telescope and a camera</strong>: aperture, magnification, resolution, mounts, exposures, calibration frames, stacking and honest processing.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Every lesson starts with the big idea and what to read first, then gives you a step-by-step "watch it happen" player, a simulation to play with, a box on what each symbol means physically, a worked example, live problems with fresh numbers, hints and full solutions, a common mix-up, key points you can download as a summary sheet, a short quiz, and links to the free <a href="/science/astronomy/">astronomy tools</a> on fibub so you can try it under the real sky. When you want to know how stars and galaxies work, go on to <a href="/learn/courses/astronomy/">Astronomy</a>.</p>
  </section>
</CourseHome>
